    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d731">

                <pb facs="1000" n="986" xml:id="pg986"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.544/67: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-15T09:00:00+07:00">April 15, 1944—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>658. Department’s 310, March 7, 6 p.m. Copy of draft revision of copyright law
                    being airmailed.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d731-f1"/> Understood to have been passed
                    by Legislative Yuan March 31 but not yet promulgated. No radical changes made in
                    existing law.</p>
                <p>According to records of Economic Affairs Ministry and Legislative Yuan, no
                    amendment to company law has been promulgated. Regulations governing special
                    limited corporations were promulgated March 1940. Copy being airmailed.<anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d731-f2"/> Registration fees were increased 900% June 9,
                    1943.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
